---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Contact World Battery Hub';
const description = 'Contact World Battery Hub — request a quote for the lead-acid product catalogue, send editorial corrections, or ask data and methodology questions. Contact details are placeholders pending final setup.';
const canonical = '/contact/';

const contactJsonLd = {
  '@type': 'ContactPage',
  name: title,
  url: 'https://worldbatteryhub.com/contact/',
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  ogType="website"
  jsonLd={[contactJsonLd]}
  author="World Battery Hub"
  dateModified="2026-10-23"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="byline">Contact · Last reviewed 2026-10-23</p>
      <h1>Contact World Battery Hub</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Three contact paths, one of which is primary: the commercial RFQ route for the product catalogue, the
        editorial correction route, and the data and methodology route. This page also states what you can
        realistically expect in response.
      </p>

      <div class="takeaways">
        <strong>At a glance:</strong> The <a href="/lead-acid/products/">lead-acid product catalogue</a> is the
        platform's commercial section and its <strong>request-a-quote (RFQ)</strong> route is the primary
        contact channel. The email addresses below are <strong>placeholders pending final setup</strong>; they
        are shown here honestly as placeholders, not presented as live inboxes. Until final addresses are
        published, treat this page as the routing map rather than a guaranteed response channel.
      </div>

      <h2 id="rfq">Request a quote (RFQ) — primary channel</h2>
      <p>
        The platform's commercial section is the
        <a href="/lead-acid/products/">lead-acid product catalogue</a>, covering bulk supply, private
        labelling, and OEM/ODM programmes. Pricing is quotation-based: no price list is published, and no price
        on this site is an offer.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Email:</strong> rfq@worldbatteryhub.com <span class="muted">(placeholder — final address pending)</span></p>
      <p>
        <strong>To get a useful response, include:</strong> the model or group size you need; the quantity and
        target market; the required certifications; and the delivery region. A complete inquiry is routed and
        answered faster than a bare "send me a price list" message.
      </p>

      <h2 id="editorial">Editorial corrections &amp; data problems</h2>
      <p>
        Found an incorrect specification, an outdated source, or a data error? Report it through this route.
        Corrections are recorded as <em>original value / corrected value / reason / date</em>, per the site's
        <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Email:</strong> editorial@worldbatteryhub.com <span class="muted">(placeholder — final address pending)</span></p>
      <p>
        <strong>Include:</strong> the page URL, the current value and the corrected value, and (if you have
        one) a source for the correction. A report with a source is triaged against primary material and can be
        actioned quickly; a report without a source is investigated before any change is made.
      </p>

      <h2>Data &amp; methodology questions</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about dataset methodology, source provenance, evidence status, or the
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a> dataset licence, and data-licensing
        or integration enquiries, go through this route.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Email:</strong> data@worldbatteryhub.com <span class="muted">(placeholder — final address pending)</span></p>

      <h2>What you can expect</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to acknowledge routine enquiries within a few business days and to route RFQs promptly. This is a
        reasonable-effort target, not a contractual service level: the contact addresses are placeholders until
        final setup, and once final addresses are live this page will state a firmer response commitment.
      </p>
      <p>
        To keep responses fast and correct, send one topic per message. An RFQ, a correction report and a data
        question are three different routes and are handled by different people.
      </p>

      <h2>What this page does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No purchasing advice</strong> — RFQ responses are quotation-based; the platform does not
            recommend a battery for your installation.</li>
        <li><strong>No published price lists</strong> — pricing is given only in response to an RFQ.</li>
        <li><strong>No telephone or physical address</strong> — none is published yet, because the operator's
            legal entity and contact details are <a href="/about/#operator-disclosure">pending confirmation</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>No technical support</strong> — engineering and installation questions are outside the
            platform's scope; see the <a href="/safety-notice/">Safety Notice</a> and your manufacturer's
            documentation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Related pages</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/about/">About</a> — the platform, its editorial method and operator disclosure.</li>
        <li><a href="/lead-acid/products/">Product catalogue</a> — the commercial RFQ section.</li>
        <li><a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> — how content is researched, verified and corrected.</li>
        <li><a href="/data-use-and-citation/">Data Use &amp; Citation</a> — reuse and citation terms.</li>
        <li><a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> — what we do with what you send us.</li>
        <li><a href="/terms-of-use/">Terms of Use</a> — the terms governing this site.</li>
        <li><a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> — the limits of what we claim.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
